{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And your seed shall be as the dust of the earth, and you shall spread out.</b> After your seed shall have become as the dust of the earth, in the manner of וַתָּשִׂימִי כָאָרֶץ גֵּוֵךְ וְכַחוּץ לָעוֹבְרִים (Isaiah 51:23) — that is, when they are at the utmost extremity of lowliness — then you shall burst forth in <b>the land upon which you lie</b> in every direction: <b>westward and eastward and northward and southward</b>. For indeed the future salvation of El will come after an unprecedented depth of Israel's lowliness such as exists today in their exile. As the Sages, of blessed memory, said: If you see a generation upon which troubles come sweeping like a river, await him, as it says: כִּי יָבֹא כַנָּהָר צָר, and the verse next to it reads: וּבָא לְצִיּוֹן גּוֹאֵל (Isaiah 59:19–20)." "<b>And in you shall all the families of the earth be blessed, and in your seed.</b> In the manner of וְאַתֶּם כֹּהֲנֵי יהוה תִּקָּרֵאוּ, מְשָׁרְתֵי אֱלֹהֵינוּ יֵאָמֵר לָכֶם (Isaiah 61:6)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:12.660620044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}